              <data key="d100">Interferon gamma</data>
              <data key="d101">Immune interferon</data>
              <data key="d104">Type II interferon produced by immune cells such as T-cells and NK cells that plays crucial roles in antimicrobial, antiviral, and antitumor responses by activating effector immune cells and enhancing antigen presentation. Primarily signals through the JAK-STAT pathway after interaction with its receptor IFNGR1 to affect gene regulation.</data>
              <data key="d105">Secreted</data>
              <data key="d107">HGNC:5438</data>
